<link rel="stylesheet" href="/OpenForum/AddOn/ContentEditor/PageConverter/page.css?ts=&time;"/>
<div class="pc">
  <header class="pc-head">
    <a class="pc-back" href="/OpenForum/AddOn/ContentEditor">← Content Editor</a>
    <h1>Import a page into the Content Editor</h1>
    <p>Turns an existing Development page into a content page or blog article you can edit, save and publish in the Content Editor. Importing only adds the editor's own files: the page shows its old content until you publish it from the editor, and its original page.content and data.json are kept beside it.</p>
  </header>
  <form class="pc-form" id="pc-form" autocomplete="off">
    <label for="pc-page">Page</label>
    <input id="pc-page" type="text" spellcheck="false" placeholder="/YourPage"/>
    <fieldset class="pc-types">
      <legend>Import as</legend>
      <label><input type="radio" name="pc-type" value="content-page" checked/> Content page</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="pc-type" value="blog-article"/> Blog article</label>
    </fieldset>
    <button class="pc-btn" type="submit">Check</button>
  </form>
  <div id="pc-result" class="pc-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
  <div class="pc-frames">
    <figure><figcaption>The page now</figcaption><iframe id="pc-original" title="The page now"></iframe></figure>
    <figure><figcaption>Imported into the template</figcaption><iframe id="pc-preview" title="The imported page" sandbox=""></iframe></figure>
  </div>
</div>

